\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The refinement dilemma, drawn to scale for the test split (shares of 513 pairs; C: certified; the residual is the fragment the judge decides). Refinement enlarges the refuted region, which removes pairs from the judge's jurisdiction and closes the prose-only injection class. Because the calibration pool is the distinct part of the residual, the pool shrinks with it (primary judge: from 142 to 49 pairs), and at $\alpha =0.05$ the conformal threshold moves from the 7th to the 2nd largest pool score (Proposition~\ref {prop:dilemma}). Section~\ref {sec:res-refinement} measures the consequence.}}{25}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:refinement}{{1}{25}{The refinement dilemma, drawn to scale for the test split (shares of 513 pairs; C: certified; the residual is the fragment the judge decides). Refinement enlarges the refuted region, which removes pairs from the judge's jurisdiction and closes the prose-only injection class. Because the calibration pool is the distinct part of the residual, the pool shrinks with it (primary judge: from 142 to 49 pairs), and at $\alpha =0.05$ the conformal threshold moves from the 7th to the 2nd largest pool score (Proposition~\ref {prop:dilemma}). Section~\ref {sec:res-refinement} measures the consequence}{figure.1}{}}
