\def\@LN@column{1}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Why the correction is needed. Monte-Carlo simulation with exchangeable continuous scores, calibration pool $n=200$, $\alpha =0.05$, 2,000 replications per $m$: the probability that a request distinct from all $m$ candidates is suppressed. The uncorrected rule reaches 89.0\% at $m=50$. The corrected rule stays within Monte-Carlo error of $\alpha $ and switches semantic suppression off once $m$ exceeds the budget $\alpha (n+1)$, which is the intended failure direction.}}{61}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:multiplicity}{{5}{61}{Why the correction is needed. Monte-Carlo simulation with exchangeable continuous scores, calibration pool $n=200$, $\alpha =0.05$, 2,000 replications per $m$: the probability that a request distinct from all $m$ candidates is suppressed. The uncorrected rule reaches 89.0\% at $m=50$. The corrected rule stays within Monte-Carlo error of $\alpha $ and switches semantic suppression off once $m$ exceeds the budget $\alpha (n+1)$, which is the intended failure direction}{figure.5}{}}
