\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Adversarial injection on the 45 held-out attack pairs (all distinct acts; every suppression is wrong), with 95\% Wilson intervals. Calibration offers no protection under deliberate shift. The refuter removes D4a on every judge by construction (the zeros are logical, not estimated). On D4b the typed fields agree, the refuter is silent, and the outcome is whatever the judge does, until the refined (tightened) declaration types the distinguishing numbers. Theorem~\ref {thm:bound} does not apply to this split.}}{66}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:adversarial}{{6}{66}{Adversarial injection on the 45 held-out attack pairs (all distinct acts; every suppression is wrong), with 95\% Wilson intervals. Calibration offers no protection under deliberate shift. The refuter removes D4a on every judge by construction (the zeros are logical, not estimated). On D4b the typed fields agree, the refuter is silent, and the outcome is whatever the judge does, until the refined (tightened) declaration types the distinguishing numbers. Theorem~\ref {thm:bound} does not apply to this split}{figure.6}{}}
